														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4846763">
									

<p>Thanks for the suggestion, that did get me thinking about the stakes more. For the hook, maybe instead of being able to reuse element A's, you'd have to constantly change element A, and if you reuse one element in a whole teleportation cycle, it will teleport. Maybe that would raise the stakes significantly, and it becomes a time bomb that still needs maintenance instead of essentially trash disposal that would need to alternate between food waste and aluminum &amp; glass. Instead of testing, it could be notable objects, with results that may not be immediately obvious.</p>
<p>For the why, I feel it could be a weapon from the reality bender, a big middle finger to the earth, because eventually the spire would wipe out all matter on earth, and would be difficult to contain, not including the time bomb of it eventually needing to go off from the repetition I mentioned above.</p>
<p>What would you think of these changes?</p>

